{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-pwmg-mvjw-4m23","cve_id":"CVE-2026-55084","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/security-advisories/GHSA-pwmg-mvjw-4m23","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core/security/advisories/GHSA-pwmg-mvjw-4m23","summary":" SQL Injection in SqlView Filter Parameter Leading to Arbitrary Database Read","description":"## Summary\r\n\r\nA SQL injection vulnerability was identified in the **SqlView API endpoint** of the DHIS2 application.\r\nThe vulnerability exists in the `filter` parameter used by the endpoint:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/api/sqlViews/{viewId}/data.json\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis behavior enables attackers to extract arbitrary database content using error-based SQL injection.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Affected Endpoint\r\n\r\n```\r\nGET /api/sqlViews/{viewId}/data.json\r\n```\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/api/sqlViews/qMYMT0iUGkG/data.json\r\n```\r\n\r\nParameters:\r\n\r\n```\r\nfilter\r\nvar\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Severity\r\n\r\n**Critical**\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability allows attackers to execute arbitrary SQL queries and extract sensitive information directly from the database.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Attack Requirements\r\n\r\nThe attacker must have:\r\n\r\n* An authenticated session\r\n* Access to any SqlView endpoint\r\n\r\nNo administrative privileges are required.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\n\r\nThe application builds SQL expressions using the user-controlled `filter` parameter without proper sanitization or query parameterization.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Reporter\r\n\r\n```\r\nSecurity Researcher\r\nAhmed Najeh\r\n```\r\n\r\n","severity":"high","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"netroms","id":145733,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NTczMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145733?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/netroms","html_url":"https://github.com/netroms","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/netroms/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/netroms/following{/other_user}","gi